\f0\fs24 \cf2 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 In the twilight, a plague came up from the south \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
over the Jamison Valley \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 to Sublime Point first as a swarm of lights, then as a choir of mosquitoes, and the mozzies became louder as the lights grew larger and brighter. \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
There was no hail, nor frogs, nor locusts. Just drones with very pretty lights.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 <!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 The remnants of the retreating UDF looked up as the drones slowed and hung in station beyond the lookout. So did Shakti security forces, the last of the dancers in the car park, and the carousers and story-tellers around campfires.\
The lights moved slowly in coherent arcs, and ranks and files, then accelerated to a flurry before resolving into famous Ulyssians from the dawn of technology. The image of Kylie Minogue received rounds of cheers and applause. Some drones darted west and cycled through the Hemsworths; Kylie became Margot Robbie. To the east, Steve Irwin delighted the viewers, though Bert Newton received head scratches, as did Con the Fruiterer and a long-gone prime minister drinking a yardglass of pissy Oxford ale in eleven seconds.\
Many more celebrities were depicted with astonishing accuracy. Yet within minutes, as had been the case for centuries with such drone and fireworks displays, the audience became bored and began wondering how long it would be before the final crescendo.\
It never came\'97at least not in a form anyone on the ground might expect. The lights went out; moments later a huge credit appeared in the sky that could have stretched across the whole valley:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qc\partightenfactor0

