\f0 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 With their lights off, the drones swarmed into the Sublime Point compound's airspace and immediately came under fire from its automated lasers. Dozens fell in the first few seconds; Fridge Force had deployed the bulk of the drones as laser cannon fodder, decoys intended to overwhelm the defence\'92s software and draw fire away from a mission-critical minimum of two groups of five drones carrying offensive payloads.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 A first pentad of drones split from the swarm and flew evasively lower, arranging themselves  continuously negotiating fluid formations as they went. Distances between them ranged from centimetres, to metres as did their elevations. Their relative positions resolved for fractions of a second into geometries whose significance was obvious only to the machines and a small number of Fridge Force physicists who had long ago stopped being invited to normal parties.\
The Sublime Point lasers calculated a solution in milliseconds and vaporised the five of them simultaneously. Another pentad broke from the swarm and came at their objective from the west. Three of them quickly ceased to exist; the remaining pair broke away and rejoined the swarm.\
Eloise had never been modest about the quality of her defences at Sublime Point. Whatever Fridge Force knew about stasis, Shakti Enterprises remained extremely competent at reducing flying objects into the scent of fresh air and fried electrical circuits.
\f0\fs24 <!$Scr_Ps::1>}